 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfQcB1Eox9Z/",
 "title": "Master Your Sales Script Like the Top 0.01%",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains that sounding like you are reading a script means you do not know it well enough. He shares an exercise using two printed copies of your script to master it completely so you can focus on the prospect instead of what you are saying.",
 "key_points": [
  "If you sound like you are reading a script, it is because you do not know the script well enough.",
  "Print out two versions of your script: one to correct from and one to read from.",
  "Read the script out loud, enunciating every word clearly.",
  "Cross out one word, then read the document again with that word missing.",
  "Go back to the top, black out a second word, and read it again.",
  "Repeat this process until every word in the script is crossed out and you are saying the script from a blank page.",
  "When selling, you should not be thinking about what you are going to say, but about what the prospect is saying, because a lot of sales happen in your ears, not your mouth."
 ],
 "content": "MASTER THE SCRIPT LIKE THE TOP 0.01% ALEX HORMOZI $250M/Year Founder, Acquisition.com If you sound like you're reading a script, the reality is it's because you don't know the script well enough. You print out two versions of your script: the script you correct yourself from and then the script you read from. You're going to read it out loud, enunciating every word clearly, that's it. And then you'll cross out one of the words, and then you will read that document again with the word missing. Then, when you get to the bottom, you'll go back to the top and you'll black out a second word, and then you'll read it again. And by the end of this process, you will have repeated the script as many times as there are words in the script. At the end, you'll be looking at a blank page that has all blacked out words, and you'll be saying the script. The reason this is important is because if you are selling, the last thing you should be thinking about is what you're going to say. You should be thinking about what the prospect is saying, because a lot of sales is in your ears, not from your mouth. 5 Steps to solving 99% of sales issues: 1) Actually have an offer not just “buy my thing” 2) Have a written script 3) Practice the script daily (don’t allow off script sales) 4) Respond to leads immediately 5) Sell to richer customers Actually do them rather than nod along.",
